---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../config/site';
const p = SITE.publisher;
---
<Base title="About and funding" description="Who publishes this site, how it is funded, and the standards it holds itself to.">
  <div class="wrap-narrow pt-10 md:pt-14">
    <p class="eyebrow">About and funding</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-2 text-[clamp(34px,4.6vw,52px)]">Who’s behind this, and why you can check everything</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>{SITE.name} exists so that anyone, whether a parent at the kitchen table, a journalist on deadline or a student, can find out how the country is going without wading through a dozen government websites, and without being told what to think.</p>
      <h2>Our standards</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Official figures only.</strong> Every number comes from an official publisher and links to the page it came from.</li>
        <li><strong>Verdicts only on real commitments.</strong> The government is judged against what it said it would do, under rules published in full. Everything else is shown without a verdict.</li>
        <li><strong>The same rules for whoever governs.</strong> The rules don’t mention a party. When the government changes, the same yardsticks apply to the next one.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain words.</strong> No jargon without an explanation, and no adjectives doing the work of evidence.</li>
        <li><strong>Mistakes are fixed in public.</strong> See the <a href={url('corrections/')}>corrections log</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who publishes it and who pays</h2>
      {p ? <><p><strong>{p.name}.</strong> {p.statement}</p><p>{p.funding}</p><p>Contact: {p.contact}</p></>
        : <p class="rounded-lg bg-warn-tint p-4 text-[15.5px] text-warn"><strong>Being finalised before launch.</strong> This section will name the publisher, state any political memberships or affiliations of the people involved, and say exactly who funds the site. A site that asks for your trust owes you that, and this one won’t launch without it.</p>}
      <h2>What we won’t do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Take money from political parties, or let any funder see or shape a verdict before it’s published.</li>
        <li>Run advertising that tracks you. The site sets no tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>Sell or share subscriber email addresses.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href={url('corrections/#report')}>report form</a> for errors, missing commitments or anything else. Every message is read.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
